    The code generator compiles a local function as a closure, recursive and mutually recursive within its block (row 304)

    The team's code generator refused every local function ('Can't compile LetFn'), though the specification allows local functions with the syntax of top-level ones, walk binds each as a closure in the block's environment, and nine declarations of the interpreter's library stopped there after the checker passed them. Each local function now compiles as a closure class made as a function expression's, reaching itself as its own this and its siblings through fields the block sets once, so the group needs no mutable cell; under the switch-over's setting the code generator's refusals over the fourteen components fall from 47 in 11 kinds to 38 in 10, and row 304 narrows to the three forms still refused (static parameters of its own, overloading within a block, atomic), each with its XXX test.

    Climb batch 26, rung L (rung-codegen-local-functions), gathered from wip/rung-codegen-local-functions.
    historical: ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/compiler/codegen/CodeGen.java

    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
